{"subjectId":"dsa-basics","id":"circular_linked","title":"Circular Linked List","group":"","order":12,"html":"<p>10 --&gt; 5 --&gt; 20 --&gt; 15 --&gt; goes to first element</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Node:\n    def __init__(self, data):\n        self.data = data\n        self.next = None\n\nhead = Node(10)\nhead.next = Node(5)\nhead.next.next = Node(20)\nhead.next.next.next = Node(15)\nhead.next.next.next.next = head\n\ntemp = head\nwhile temp.next != head:\n    print(temp.data)\n    temp = temp.next\nprint(temp.data)</code></pre></figure>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3>Advantages</h3>\n<p>1. We can traverse the whole list from any node</p>\n<p>2. Implementation of Algorithms like Round Robin</p>\n<p>3. We can insert at the beginning and end by just maintaining one tail reference/pointer</p>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Disadvantages</h3>\n<p>1. Implementation of operations becomes complex</p>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Traversing</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Implementation\n\ndef printCircular(head):\n  if head == None:\n    return\n\n  print(head.data, end = \" \")\n  curr = head.next\n  while curr != head:\n    print(curr.data, end=\" \")\n    curr = curr.next\n\nhead = Node(10)\nhead.next = Node(5)\nhead.next.next = Node(20)\nhead.next.next.next = Node(15)\nhead.next.next.next.next = head\n\nprintCircular(head)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Insert at beginning</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 1 (Linear Time)\n\ndef insertBag(head, x):\n  temp = Node(x)\n  if head == None:\n    temp.next = temp\n    return temp\n  curr = head\n  while curr.next != head:\n    curr = curr.next\n  curr.next = temp\n  temp.next = head\n  return temp\n\nhead = insertBag(head, 25)\nprintCircular(head)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 2 (Constant Time)\n\ndef insertBag(head, x):\n  temp = Node(x)\n  if head == None:\n    temp.next = temp\n    return temp\n  temp.next = head.next\n  head.next = temp\n  head.data, temp.data = temp.data, head.data\n  return head\n\nhead = insertBag(head, 30)\nprintCircular(head)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Insert at End</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef insertEnd(head, x):\n  temp = Node(x)\n  if head == None:\n    temp.next = temp\n    return temp\n  curr = head\n  while curr.next != head:\n    curr = curr.next\n  curr.next = temp\n  temp.next = head\n  return head\n\nhead = insertEnd(head, 35)\nprintCircular(head)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef insertEnd(head, x):\n  temp = Node(x)\n  if head == None:\n    temp.next = temp\n    return temp\n  temp.next = head.next\n  head.next = temp\n  head.data, temp.data = temp.data, head.data\n  return temp\n\nhead = insertEnd(head, 40)\nprintCircular(head)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Delete head</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef delHead(head):\n  if head == None:\n    return None\n  elif head.next == head:\n    return None\n  curr = head\n  while curr.next != head:\n    curr = curr.next\n\n  curr.next = head.next\n  return curr.next\n\nhead = delHead(head)\nprintCircular(head)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef delHead(head):\n  if head == None:\n    return None\n  elif head.next == head:\n    return None\n  head.data = head.next.data\n  head.next = head.next.next\n  return head\n\nhead = delHead(head)\nprintCircular(head)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Delete kth Node</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def delkthNode(head, k):\n  if head == None:\n    return None\n\n  elif k == 1:\n    return delHead(head)\n\n  curr = head\n  for i in range(1, k-2):\n    curr = curr.next\n  curr.next = curr.next.next\n  return head\n\nhead = delkthNode(head, 2)\nprintCircular(head)</code></pre></figure></section>"}